WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:16.908
Josh ran upstairs to tell Molly's mom about Molly's accident.

2
00:00:16.909 --> 00:00:21.040
Mrs. O'Donnell rushed down the stairs in front of our building.

3
00:00:21.041 --> 00:00:23.190
Molly tried to get up.

4
00:00:23.191 --> 00:00:25.773
But she couldn't stand on her right foot.

5
00:00:25.774 --> 00:00:29.846
"Ow! It really hurts!" she cried.

6
00:00:29.847 --> 00:00:33.740
"Don't try to stand on it!" said Molly's mom.

7
00:00:33.741 --> 00:00:38.161
"I think we'd better take a taxi to the hospital."

8
00:00:38.162 --> 00:00:43.830
Mr. Calabria went out to the street and stopped a taxi.

9
00:00:43.831 --> 00:00:48.479
Then Molly, her mom, and Caswell got inside.

10
00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.926
Caswell waved to us as the taxi sped away.

11
00:00:52.927 --> 00:00:58.374
He was still licking his lime ice pop.

12
00:00:58.375 --> 00:01:04.143
Josh, Jenny, and I ran upstairs and told my mom about Molly's accident.

13
00:01:04.144 --> 00:01:08.221
A short time later, Mr. Chen came to our door.

14
00:01:08.222 --> 00:01:12.535
Josh and Jenny's aunt, Lydia, was with him.

15
00:01:12.536 --> 00:01:15.564
I had met Aunt Lydia before.

16
00:01:15.565 --> 00:01:19.495
She looked like Mr. Chen, but she was taller.

17
00:01:19.496 --> 00:01:22.141
She also laughed a lot.

18
00:01:22.142 --> 00:01:26.842
She laughed now as she leaned over to hug Josh and Jenny.

19
00:01:26.843 --> 00:01:30.382
"I want you to meet someone," she said.

20
00:01:30.383 --> 00:01:33.286
"He's waiting for you downstairs."

21
00:01:33.287 --> 00:01:35.332
She smiled at me.

22
00:01:35.333 --> 00:01:38.612
"Iggy, you can come too!"

23
00:01:38.613 --> 00:01:42.503
We went downstairs to Josh and Jenny's apartment.

24
00:01:42.504 --> 00:01:50.302
There, sitting on the kitchen table, was a cage with a brightly colored parrot!

25
00:01:50.303 --> 00:01:54.452
"This is my parrot, Tufty," Aunt Lydia said.

26
00:01:54.453 --> 00:01:58.029
She smiled at Josh and Jenny.

27
00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:02.193
"I am moving to California," she explained.

28
00:02:02.194 --> 00:02:06.845
"I can't take my Tufty with me so I'm giving him to you two."

29
00:02:06.846 --> 00:02:09.727
Jenny's eyes lit up.

30
00:02:09.728 --> 00:02:14.123
"Can we really keep Tufty, Dad?" she asked.

31
00:02:14.124 --> 00:02:20.188
Mr. Chen nodded. "Aunt Lydia says he's quiet and well-behaved."

32
00:02:20.189 --> 00:02:25.001
Bunch sniffed at the cage and wagged his tail.

33
00:02:25.002 --> 00:02:29.180
"Bunch likes Tufty!" said Josh.

34
00:02:29.181 --> 00:02:35.023
Aunt Lydia opened the birdcage.

35
00:02:35.024 --> 00:02:39.050
Tufty flew to Jenny and landed on her shoulder.

36
00:02:39.051 --> 00:02:43.119
"And Tufty likes me!" cried Jenny.

37
00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:50.123
Tufty was quiet, but he was lots of fun.

38
00:02:50.124 --> 00:02:55.630
We played with him while we waited for Molly to come home from the hospital.

39
00:02:55.631 --> 00:03:00.662
Finally we heard a car pull up.

40
00:03:00.663 --> 00:03:03.807
We ran to the window and saw a taxi.

41
00:03:03.808 --> 00:03:06.812
Molly climbed out slowly.

42
00:03:06.813 --> 00:03:10.713
She was wearing a big boot on her foot.

43
00:03:10.714 --> 00:03:15.684
Josh, Jenny, and I hurried downstairs to meet her.

44
00:03:15.685 --> 00:03:19.581
"I broke a bone in my foot," said Molly.

45
00:03:19.582 --> 00:03:24.485
"The doctor says I have to wear this walking boot until it heals."

46
00:03:24.486 --> 00:03:30.565
"If it doesn't heal, Molly will need an operation!" said Caswell.

47
00:03:30.566 --> 00:03:33.643
Molly nodded, looking upset.

48
00:03:33.644 --> 00:03:37.587
"The doctor would have to put screws in my foot!"

49
00:03:37.588 --> 00:03:42.520
"With Mr. Calabria's screwdriver?" asked Caswell.

50
00:03:42.521 --> 00:03:45.211
Molly rolled her eyes.

51
00:03:45.212 --> 00:03:48.682
"No, Caswell," she said.

52
00:03:48.683 --> 00:03:53.080
"The doctor isn't going to use Mr. Calabria's screwdriver."

53
00:03:53.081 --> 00:03:58.790
Molly frowned. "I don't want an operation!"

54
00:03:58.791 --> 00:04:02.432
We told Molly about Tufty.

55
00:04:02.433 --> 00:04:06.306
Then we all went upstairs to Molly's apartment.

56
00:04:06.307 --> 00:04:14.710
Molly walked very slowly, taking one step at a time.

57
00:04:14.711 --> 00:04:19.194
"Remember what Dr. Chang said, Molly," said Mrs. O'Donnell.

58
00:04:19.195 --> 00:04:22.018
"You have to take care of your foot.

59
00:04:22.019 --> 00:04:26.182
And if you keep your spirits up, that will help your foot to heal quickly.

60
00:04:26.183 --> 00:04:29.221
Then you won't need an operation."

61
00:04:29.222 --> 00:04:34.401
"What does 'keeping your spirits up' mean?" asked Jenny.

62
00:04:34.402 --> 00:04:39.306
"It means staying happy and cheerful," said Molly's mom.

63
00:04:39.307 --> 00:04:44.848
"It's hard to be cheerful with this walking boot on," Molly complained.

64
00:04:44.849 --> 00:04:48.269
"It makes my leg hot and itchy."

65
00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:52.032
She leaned over and scratched her leg.

66
00:04:52.033 --> 00:04:57.902
"Iggy, think of something to help Molly stay cheerful," said Caswell.

67
00:04:57.903 --> 00:05:03.313
"Yeah!" said Josh. "You have to invent something for her."

68
00:05:03.314 --> 00:05:07.083
"Something wonderful," added Jenny.

69
00:05:07.084 --> 00:05:11.149
"And different," said Molly.

70
00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:14.161
Everyone was looking at me.

71
00:05:14.162 --> 00:05:17.201
"Oh boy," I thought.

72
00:05:17.202 --> 00:05:21.600
My friends really believed in me and my powers of invention.

73
00:05:21.601 --> 00:05:29.313
Now I had to think of something to help Molly!
